## Non-Negotiable Calculation Rules

Violating any of these creates silent data errors. Do not deviate without an explicit decision logged in the spec.

### Revenue column
```
✅ gross_revenue
❌ net_owner_revenue — this column no longer exists (renamed Sprint 11)
```
Net owner revenue is computed at query time only when pm_fee_pct is known:
`gross_revenue * (1 - pm_fee_pct)` — never stored, never used as a base metric.

### Nights column
```
✅ (check_out::date - check_in::date)  — computed inline every time
❌ nights  — this column does not exist in the bookings table
```

### Cross-month booking proration — REQUIRED on every revenue/nights query
Every query summing revenue or counting nights must use the overlap formula.
Never attribute full booking values to a single period when a booking crosses a month boundary.

```sql
-- Overlap days
overlap_days = LEAST(check_out::date, period_end::date)
             - GREATEST(check_in::date, period_start::date)

-- Prorated revenue
prorated_revenue = gross_revenue
  * (LEAST(check_out::date, period_end::date)
     - GREATEST(check_in::date, period_start::date))::numeric
  / (check_out::date - check_in::date)::numeric

-- Booking inclusion filter (always include all three conditions)
check_in < period_end
AND check_out > period_start
AND check_in < CURRENT_DATE   -- excludes future bookings
```

### Future bookings
```
✅ Stored in bookings table as-is
✅ Excluded from all analytics via: check_in < CURRENT_DATE
❌ Never appear in any closed-period revenue, occupancy, ADR, or RevPAR calculation
```

### Available nights denominator
```
available_nights = calendar_nights
                 − planned_owner_stay_nights    (is_planned_owner_stay = true, booked ≥14 days prior)
                 − owner_guest_nights           (block_type = 'owner_guest')
                 − maintenance_nights           (block_type = 'maintenance')
```
Last-minute owner stays (booked <14 days prior) are NOT subtracted — they reduce revenue but not the denominator.

### Portfolio RevPAR
```
✅ SUM(revenue) / SUM(available_nights)  — available-nights-weighted
❌ AVG(property_revpar)                  — never average the averages
```

### Denominators — must never be swapped
```
✅ RevPAR denominator = available_nights
✅ ADR denominator    = prorated_booked_nights (guestBookedNights)
❌ Swapping these causes RevPAR > ADR — a mathematically impossible result (caught Sprint 16)
```

### computePeriodStats — async, always await
```
✅ Always await computePeriodStats(...)
✅ Call sites use useEffect + state pattern
❌ useMemo — computePeriodStats is async; useMemo does not support async functions
```
Applies to both app/dashboard/page.tsx and app/dashboard/analytics/page.tsx.

### Benchmark metrics
```
benchmark_occ    — stored as 0–100 percentage scale. Use as-is. DO NOT divide by 100.
benchmark_adr    — stored as day-weighted rate. Use as-is.
benchmark_revpar — stored as day-weighted rate. Use as-is.
```
All three are day-weighted rates, not daily fractions. Aggregation uses day-weighted average:
```sql
SUM(benchmark_revpar * overlap_days) / NULLIF(SUM(overlap_days), 0)
```

### market_benchmarks — no date columns, derive from week_number + year
```
❌ week_start_date — this column does not exist
❌ days_in_period  — this column does not exist
```
Always derive ISO week bounds using:
```sql
to_date(year::text || '-' || week_number::text, 'IYYY-IW')         -- Monday of ISO week (week_start)
to_date(year::text || '-' || week_number::text, 'IYYY-IW') + 7     -- exclusive week end
```
Overlap days for a week intersecting a period:
```sql
GREATEST(0,
  LEAST(week_end, period_end::date) - GREATEST(week_start, period_start::date)
) AS overlap_days
```

### market_benchmarks — submarket vs. market-level query
```
✅ Submarket-level: WHERE market_id = :market_id AND submarket_id = :submarket_id
✅ Market-level:    WHERE market_id = :market_id AND submarket_id IS NULL
❌ Never mix submarket and market-level rows in the same aggregation
```
`properties.airdna_submarket_id` — populated via zip lookup from `submarket_zip_codes`.
NULL = submarket not resolved → fall back to market-level benchmark.

### Benchmark chart guard — applies to BOTH analytics page and dashboard
Only include benchmark weeks where the week's Monday month has `data_complete = true`
in `property_coverage_months`. Derive week_start from week_number + year (no date column exists).

```sql
WITH week_bounds AS (
  SELECT mb.*,
    to_date(mb.year::text || '-' || mb.week_number::text, 'IYYY-IW') AS week_start
  FROM market_benchmarks mb
  WHERE mb.market_id = :market_id
    AND mb.source    = 'airdna_api'
)
-- Coverage guard JOIN — use month of week_start (Monday)
JOIN property_coverage_months pcm
  ON  pcm.property_id    = :property_id
  AND pcm.coverage_year  = EXTRACT(year  FROM week_bounds.week_start)::int
  AND pcm.coverage_month = EXTRACT(month FROM week_bounds.week_start)::int
  AND pcm.data_complete  = true
```
An ISO week spanning two months is attributed to the month its Monday falls in.

### Coverage completeness — Case 1 / Case 2 (built Sprint 18)
Logic lives in `lib/coverage-completeness.ts`. Evaluate per property — never cross-property.

```
Case 1 — flip data_complete = true immediately on upload:
  Last booking checkout date is in a future month (crosses boundary)
  AND upload_date >= that booking's check_in date (guest has checked in)

Case 2 — flip data_complete = true when calendar closes:
  Last booking checkout is within the current month being evaluated
  OR last booking crosses boundary but upload_date < check_in (cancellation still possible)
  → data_complete = true only when CURRENT_DATE >= first day of following month
```
Re-evaluation pass runs on dashboard load — flips eligible Case 2 months without requiring re-upload.
Soft note at portfolio level when `CURRENT_DATE >= first of following month` AND `data_complete = false`:
`"Booking data for [Month YYYY] may not be up to date — upload a new file to refresh."`

### Index card — built Sprint 17
Card order: **Gross Revenue | RevPAR | Occ% | ADR | Index**

```
Index = Math.round((property_revpar / benchmarkRevPAR) × 100)
      = — (em dash) when benchmarkRevPAR is null
```
- `benchmarkRevPAR` is returned by `computePeriodStats` as `number | null`
- No YoY delta on the Index card
- Subtext: "vs. market benchmark"
- Index currently shows — (em dash) — market_benchmarks rows are unlicensed AirDNA test data
  that must be cleared before production launch (Row 211). Index will display correctly
  once licensed benchmark data is ingested from confirmed vendor.
  Index trend + decomposition (Row 159) deferred until Row 182 complete.

